Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:04:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] M3: F6/F8 discriminating counts (DIVERGENCE-LEDGER rows
 15, 19)

holo2/measure/f6_f8_counts.py, one combined by-path driver:

(a) row 15 (F6, loser/runner-up hints): census of v1's durable
LosingHypothesis ledger on the archived e029/xerox/demo9 states plus a
spatial cross-reference against the current v1-vs-holo2 parity gap
(F2-era archived holo2 states). Measured: losers are NOT zero on the
real sheets as the ledger's own default hypothesis guessed (e029=2,
xerox=5, demo9=73) - but every retained loser on e029/xerox anchors a
tile already certified by BOTH trees, and none sits within 3 tiles
(one mop-up window span) of any current v1-only gap tile. F6's hint
arm therefore has zero measured relevance to the present e029/xerox
gap; demo9's 73 losers remain the real target population.

(b) row 19 (F8, word-pool firewall): re-derives v1's own committed-pose
pilot reads from durable PoseRecord/SurveyRegionRecord geometry (the
v0.42 place_committed/_committed_patch recipe, extended by the one call
it deliberately omits, observations_for_segment) on lane
l03-16ppc-4800dpi - native resolution, no scale-space decimation to
replicate, full tile-domain coverage. Self-validated against durable
ground truth: 0 reconstructed conflicts on both sheets, matching the
states' own AddressArtifact.bch_conflicts exactly. Pooled-vs-per-pose
known_position_words reruns differ on many tiles (131 e029, 63 xerox)
but produce zero conflicts either way on both real sheets - the
scope question is real for word decode yield, moot for the firewall's
actual conflict-detection purpose on this corpus.

Pure classification/tally logic (loser_tile_key, spatial_relevance,
f6_census, compare_pooled_vs_per_pose, summarize) pinned in
tests/holo2_oracles/test_oracle_f6_f8_counts.py on synthetic fixtures.

