holo2/measure/f7_lattice_probes.py (census|discriminator|shift, one
driver): (i) per-rung covering-window census for the xerox tx=0 residue
(17 page-edge tiles, F2 differential) — v1 draws 4.94 distinct page-cell
origins/tile across its per-lane lattices, holo2's shared lattice offers
2.00 distinct extents/tile; (ii) row 4-vs-6 discriminator, both trees'
native_affine evaluated at each tile's centre in one frame — raw delta
is 0/66 inside 1/4 cell, but a per-footing baseline correction shows the
raw number is dominated by a ~5.7-6px SYSTEMATIC per-footing frame
offset (residual stdev sub-cell at 16/1, 8/1, 4/1 once removed — the
2/1 residual stays large, consistent with c2's known sampling-limited
fits, not per-tile registration disagreement); (iii) the decisive
synthetic-offset experiment on the crop-harness runs (xerox-c01/c08/
c10/c11, copies only): 567 real WindowJob+RealPayloadWorker attempts
across the 13 still-missing target tiles (crop battery's own 4 uplifts
excluded) x 4 footings x 20 v1-style lattice-phase offsets — ZERO
shifted-window certificates (198 crc_failed, 2 below_floor), a measured
negative reinforcing (ii)'s photometry-not-registration reading for
this specific residue population.

tests/holo2_oracles/test_oracle_f7_probes.py pins the pure logic:
target-tile selection (page_edge AND tx==0, drawn from v1_only only),
shift_extent's axis-safe arithmetic, affine_point's row/column-safe
evaluation, pose_delta_cells' point-independence under a constant
offset and its loud ZeroDivisionError on ppc=0, parse_ppc's fraction
reduction, the strict (< 0.25, not <=) quarter-cell boundary, and
