holo2/measure/rf1_gate_flips.py replays every committed RF1 revision on
the two archived F2-era states (real/parity-F2/h2-{e029,xerox}) through
RF1's own gather (reach + _observed + local_segment + sample_at, frozen
generation-zero calibration replayed) and scores refine_fit.adoption_gate
two ways: (a) as shipped, marginal-only logits; (b) v1-faithful,
window-wide context-corrected logits via the pool's currently adopted
ctx fit (certified_refine._fixed_detector_logits's CONTEXT_PROFILE
branch, transcribed as ctx_corrected_logits). Measured: 89 (e029) / 148
(xerox) committed revisions in these states (not the ~270/~275 the
charge quoted — that figure is the older W2-era archived states'; the
current F2-era count is reported explicitly as a discrepancy), ZERO
gate flips on either sheet — every revision's held-out gain (min
0.17-0.18 nats) sits far above MIN_HELDOUT_GAIN (1e-4) even after
context correction shifts it by up to -0.075 nats.

Same read also answers row 54 (does _observed reassemble a pose's whole
emitted footprint? quarantine-blind vs quarantine-filtered piece union,
exhaustive over every evidence-owning pose on both sheets: zero pieces
ever dropped by quarantine; a softer support-vs-observed cardinality
sample shows the audit's own expected narrowing, ~4% median) and row 12
(RF1's photometry input: arm-A/arm-B — holo2's support-filled prepared
plane vs v1's raw-crop-no-fill sampling — on every revised window whose
footing is sub-native (raw pixels already on disk, no scan file opened):
Delta = 0.0 exactly on all 65+113 compared windows, reproducing C1-P8's
finding on RF1's own population; native-footing revisions are named but
not compared).

Pure logic pinned in tests/holo2_oracles/test_oracle_rf1_gate_flips.py:
ctx_corrected_logits against v1's own context_neighbour_counts/
apply_context_offsets calls, score_and_gate's base/candidate
directionality and its three gate clauses independently, is_flip/
quarantine_missing/support_deficit's asymmetric semantics.

