+#!/usr/bin/env python
+"""RF1's ADOPTION GATE, re-scored two ways — M1 (DIVERGENCE-LEDGER row 5).
+
+    env/bin/python holo2/measure/rf1_gate_flips.py --sheet e029
+    env/bin/python holo2/measure/rf1_gate_flips.py --sheet all \\
+        --out scratch/holo2-catchup/real/rf1-gate-flips.md
+
+NOT A TEST and not collectable as one — same standing as
+``tile_differential.py``/``rf1_resume.py`` and every other by-path driver
+in this directory (``holo2/measure/README.md``). Self-locating: needs no
+``PYTHONPATH=`` prefix.
+
+READ-ONLY, ``Store.open`` directly (never ``cli.open_receiver`` — that
+composes a live session over a recipe/source/providers, none of which a
+read-only re-score has any business constructing). Never calls anything
+that proposes a commit. Takes the state directory's exclusive lock for
+the duration of one sheet's pass (every read below needs the plane, not
+just a snapshot); do not run this against a state a decode currently has
+open. On a stale lock from a dead pid, ``Store.open`` self-heals — see
+its own docstring — this driver does not touch the lock file itself.
+
+THE CHARGE (RULINGS §N, DIVERGENCE-LEDGER row 5). RF1's own adoption gate
+(``holo2/src/holo2/solve/refine_fit.py:305-324 adoption_gate``, fired
+from ``propose()``) scores a candidate pose against v1's three-clause
+gate, but on MARGINAL-ONLY logits — ``calibration.llr(-means)``, nothing
+else. v1's gate (``src/holo/receive/certified_refine.py:702-732
+_fixed_detector_logits`` + ``_adoption_gate``) scores the SAME three
+clauses on logits corrected by the region's adopted context fit, bins
+taken over the WHOLE window's own provisional ink
+(``context_neighbour_counts(window.page_cells_yx, ...)``) — v1's window
+scope, which F1 (ledger row 2) already gave holo2 for free at RF1's own
+cell set. Row 5 asks: does re-scoring holo2's OWN committed revisions
+under v1's convention ever REFUSE what the shipped gate ADOPTED? If the
+F2/F2a receiver's +27/+32 certificates on the two real sheets rode
+revisions v1's own math would not have adopted, that yield was measured
+on a different algorithm than v1's.
+
+WHAT THIS SCRIPT DOES, per sheet, per committed RF1 revision (every
+window with exactly two committed, non-quarantined poses — the base
+generation-zero pose and the live revision RF1 minted over it):
+
+1. Re-derive the revision's own inputs EXACTLY as
+   ``refine.PoseRefineWorker._gather``/``refine_fit.propose`` do: the
+   pose's observed cells (``refine.PoseRefineWorker._observed`` over
+   ``refine.reach``'s quarantine-filtered pieces), the frozen
+   generation-zero calibration (``refine.replay_calibration``), and the
+   raw luma sampled at BOTH the base pose's geometry and the committed
+   revision's geometry, off the SAME immutable prepared plane
+   (``refine.local_segment`` + ``refine.sample_at``) — the pixels never
+   changed, so this reproduces the search's own final-candidate sample
+   bit-for-bit.
+2. Score gate (a), AS SHIPPED: marginal logits only
+   (``calibration.llr(-means)``), through ``refine_fit.adoption_gate``
+   unmodified.
+3. Score gate (b), V1-FAITHFUL: the SAME marginal logits, corrected by
+   the pool's CURRENTLY adopted context fit
+   (``ctx_apply.adopted_context_fit``) over WINDOW-WIDE bins
+   (:func:`ctx_corrected_logits`, v1's own ``_fixed_detector_logits``
+   CONTEXT_PROFILE branch, transcribed) — through the SAME
+   ``adoption_gate``. A pool with no adopted fit takes zero offsets
+   (v1's PAVA_PROFILE branch — no correction to refuse).
+4. A FLIP is gate (a) ADOPTED and gate (b) REFUSED (:func:`is_flip`;
+   directional on purpose — "adoptions v1's scoring would refuse", never
+   the symmetric difference).
+
+Both gates are counterfactual RE-SCORES on the FINAL certified frontier
+(the labels ``refine.collect_labels`` reads are today's certified cargo,
+which can only have GROWN since any one revision's own commit moment) —
+consistent with how F1's own row-1/row-2 measurement re-froze holo2's
+committed evidence (DIVERGENCE-LEDGER row 1: "re-freezes of holo2's OWN
+committed evidence"). Gate (a) is expected to reproduce ADOPTED for
+every row (a sanity check on the replay itself, printed as a warning if
+it ever does not); the question is what gate (b) then says.
+
+ALSO IN THIS SCRIPT (the same charge names rows 54 and 12, whose
+discriminating measurements are cheap extensions of the same read):
+
+* **Row 54** (a PIN, not a fix): does ``refine.PoseRefineWorker.
+  _observed``'s reassembly from evidence PIECES return the pose's WHOLE
+  emitted footprint? Two independent checks, run over every
+  evidence-owning pose (not just the revised population):
+  (:func:`quarantine_missing`) exact — the only mechanism found in the
+  source that could make the reassembly incomplete AFTER a placement's
+  all-or-nothing emission (``place_shared.emit_placement`` writes its
+  pose and every one of its tiles' pieces in ONE returned batch; a
+  refused emission writes NEITHER) is per-piece quarantine
+  (``quarantine.is_quarantined``, checked inside ``refine.reaches``) —
+  compare the union of ALL of a pose's evidence keys
+  (``refine.pose_evidence_keys``, quarantine-BLIND) against
+  ``refine.reach``'s quarantine-FILTERED set; and
+  (:func:`support_deficit`) approximate — the pose's observed cell COUNT
+  against the region's own SURVEY SUPPORT count over the window's
+  declared extent (``RegionView.support`` sliced at the window's
+  ``extent_cells``, the same arithmetic ``plans.window_plans_for`` uses
+  to decide a window is schedulable at all), reported as a deficit
+  fraction. The second check is NOT a piece-completeness proof by
+  itself — the placement AUDIT (corner defects, the straddle exclusion,
+  ``config.erode_cells``) legitimately narrows a pose's own footprint
+  below raw geometric support, and this script cannot replay that audit
+  without re-fitting the window's pose from pixels (out of scope for a
+  state-only read) — so a nonzero deficit is EXPECTED and is reported as
+  a distribution, not a pass/fail; the quarantine check is the exact
+  one.
+* **Row 12** (EQUIVALENT-UNPINNED): RF1's photometry input.
+  ``certified_refine.RefinementRegionImage``/``prepare_region_image``
+  (v1) crops RAW luma straight from the raster — NO support fill — and
+  box-filters it, ``cval`` at sample time = the CROP's own median.
+  ``plane.prepared_region`` (holo2, ``solve/prepared.py``) fills every
+  UNSUPPORTED pixel to the capture's durable ``platen_backing`` BEFORE
+  filtering, built once for the whole region. C1-P8
+  (``v1audit/c1p8_photometry.py``) already measured this arm-A/arm-B gap
+  at Δ = 0.0 for payload photometry on interior tiles; this script runs
+  the SAME two arms (:func:`sample_v1_style`) on RF1's own population —
+  every revised window whose footing is SUB-NATIVE (its raw pixels
+  already sit on disk as a derived footing raster,
+  ``capture.footing_raster.open_footing_raster`` over the SAME
+  ``<state-dir>.prepared`` sibling every other read here uses — no scan
+  file opened) — and reports the max/mean |Δ|. The NATIVE footing's
+  revisions are named but NOT compared: their raw pixels are only in the
+  original scan file, which this state-only pass does not open.
+"""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import argparse
+import json
+import sys
+from contextlib import contextmanager
+from dataclasses import asdict, dataclass
+from pathlib import Path
+from typing import Iterator, Sequence
+
+import numpy as np
+from scipy import ndimage
+
+# Self-locating, like every other by-path driver here.
+_HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
+_ROOT = _HERE.parent.parent
+for _path in (_ROOT / "holo2" / "src", _ROOT / "src"):
+    _str = str(_path)
+    if _str not in sys.path:
+        sys.path.insert(0, _str)
+
+from holo2.capture import catalog_captures                        # noqa: E402
+from holo2.capture.footing_raster import (FootingFrame,           # noqa: E402
+                                          footing_plan,
+                                          open_footing_raster)
+from holo2.cli import record_registry                              # noqa: E402
+from holo2.core import ResourceKey, Store                          # noqa: E402
+from holo2.format import format_row_for, tile_format_for           # noqa: E402
+from holo2.solve import StoreIndex, parse_window_key                # noqa: E402
+from holo2.solve import calibration as cal_mod                      # noqa: E402
+from holo2.solve import ctx_apply, detect, refine                   # noqa: E402
+from holo2.solve.certified_labels import CertifiedLabelSource       # noqa: E402
+from holo2.solve.keys import (EVIDENCE_KEY_PARTS, KIND_EVIDENCE,    # noqa: E402
+                              KIND_POSE, KIND_WINDOW, POSE_KEY_PARTS,
+                              WINDOW_KEY_PARTS)
+from holo2.solve.place_model import PlacementConfig                 # noqa: E402
+from holo2.solve.plane import capture_view                          # noqa: E402
+from holo2.solve.prepared import open_prepared_region, prepared_directory  # noqa: E402,E501
+from holo2.solve.reference import V1ReferenceField                  # noqa: E402
+
+#: v1's ``certified_refine.APERTURE_CELLS`` / holo2's own
+#: ``prepared.PLANES`` aperture convention — re-declared per the same
+#: reasoning ``refine_fit.py``'s module docstring states for its own
+#: carried constants (no ``src/holo`` import from production code; the
+#: value is pinned against v1's by ``tests/holo2_oracles/
+#: test_oracle_refine.py`` already, so a drift there is caught).
+APERTURE_CELLS = 0.7
+CTX_BINS = detect.N_CONTEXT_BINS
+
+#: The two archived F2-era states this charge names (RULINGS §N; worker
+#: instructions). Both decode the same printed identity.
+SHEETS = {
+    "e029": dict(
+        state=str(_ROOT / "scratch/holo2-catchup/real/parity-F2/h2-e029"),
+        fmt="L:c2-r0700@3392x2368"),
+    "xerox": dict(
+        state=str(_ROOT / "scratch/holo2-catchup/real/parity-F2/h2-xerox"),
+        fmt="L:c2-r0700@3392x2368"),
+}
+
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# pure logic — pinned in tests/holo2_oracles/test_oracle_rf1_gate_flips.py
+# ===========================================================================
+
+
+def ctx_corrected_logits(marginal: np.ndarray, page_cells: np.ndarray,
+                         offsets: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+    """v1's ``certified_refine._fixed_detector_logits``, CONTEXT_PROFILE
+    branch (``certified_refine.py:707-715``), transcribed once.
+
+    Bins come from the WHOLE ``page_cells``' own provisional ink
+    (``marginal > 0``) — v1's window scope, not a per-tile assembly
+    scope — and cells whose eight-neighbourhood is incomplete take bin
+    -1 (unchanged by the shared clamp kernel). No holo2 addition rides
+    along: this is the row-5 gate's v1-faithful half and nothing else.
+    """
+    counts, valid = detect.context_neighbour_counts(
+        np.asarray(page_cells, np.int64), np.asarray(marginal) > 0.0)
+    bins = np.where(valid, counts, -1).astype(np.int8)
+    return detect.apply_context_offsets(
+        np.asarray(marginal, np.float64), bins, np.asarray(offsets))
+
+
+@dataclass(frozen=True)
+class GateInputs:
+    """One revision's LABEL geometry — shared by gate (a) and gate (b).
+
+    Everything that does NOT depend on which logit convention scores it:
+    which rows are held out, which are pilots, and the two RAW pilot
+    mismatches (``refine_fit.propose``'s third gate clause is
+    deliberately detector-free — it reads ``means``, never a logit).
+    """
+
+    valid_rows: np.ndarray
+    valid_values: np.ndarray
+    valid_weights: np.ndarray
+    pilot_rows: np.ndarray
+    pilot_values: np.ndarray
+    base_raw_mismatch: float
+    cand_raw_mismatch: float
+
+
+def score_and_gate(base_logits: np.ndarray, cand_logits: np.ndarray,
+                   gi: GateInputs) -> tuple[bool, float, float]:
+    """``refine_fit.propose``'s tail, on one pair of already-scored logits.
+
+    Gate (a) [marginal] and gate (b) [v1-faithful] are the SAME call on
+    different ``base_logits``/``cand_logits`` — never two hand-written
+    copies of the loss/mismatch/gate arithmetic that could drift apart
+    from each other or from ``refine_fit.adoption_gate`` itself.
+    """
+    base_loss = refine.weighted_logloss(
+        base_logits[gi.valid_rows], gi.valid_values, gi.valid_weights)
+    cand_loss = refine.weighted_logloss(
+        cand_logits[gi.valid_rows], gi.valid_values, gi.valid_weights)
+    base_pilot_mismatch = float(np.mean(
+        (base_logits[gi.pilot_rows] > 0.0) != (gi.pilot_values > 0)))
+    cand_pilot_mismatch = float(np.mean(
+        (cand_logits[gi.pilot_rows] > 0.0) != (gi.pilot_values > 0)))
+    adopted = refine.adoption_gate(
+        base_loss, cand_loss, base_pilot_mismatch, cand_pilot_mismatch,
+        gi.base_raw_mismatch, gi.cand_raw_mismatch)
+    return adopted, base_loss, cand_loss
+
+
+def is_flip(adopted_a: bool, adopted_b: bool) -> bool:
+    """A FLIP is v1's scoring REFUSING what the shipped gate ADOPTED.
+
+    Directional on purpose (row 5's own question: "adoptions v1's
+    scoring would refuse") — never ``adopted_a != adopted_b``, which
+    would also count the (impossible under this charge, since every row
+    is a COMMITTED revision) reverse case.
+    """
+    return bool(adopted_a and not adopted_b)
+
+
+def support_deficit(support_count: int,
+                    observed_count: int) -> tuple[int, float]:
+    """(supported-but-unobserved cell count, that count / support) — row
+    54's approximate structural check. A negative deficit (more observed
+    than support) would mean the two counts are not in the same frame
+    and is surfaced rather than clamped away."""
+    deficit = int(support_count) - int(observed_count)
+    frac = (deficit / support_count) if support_count > 0 else float("nan")
+    return deficit, frac
+
+
+def quarantine_missing(all_pieces: Sequence[ResourceKey],
+                       filtered_pieces: Sequence[ResourceKey]
+                       ) -> frozenset:
+    """Pieces quarantine dropped from ``_observed``'s reconstruction.
+
+    Asymmetric on purpose: ``refine.reaches`` only ever DROPS pieces
+    (``is_quarantined`` filters), so the filtered set is a subset of the
+    full set by construction and this is ``all - filtered``, never the
+    reverse.
+    """
+    return frozenset(all_pieces) - frozenset(filtered_pieces)
+
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# the read-only plane shim
+# ===========================================================================
+
+
+class ReadOnlyPlane:
+    """The THREE methods ``refine``/``calibration``/``ctx_apply``/
+    ``certified_labels`` need for a read-only replay: ``.index()``,
+    ``.record(key)``, ``.read_array(ref)``. Not a ``SessionPlane`` — no
+    captures, no scheduling surface, no write path — and must never be
+    handed to a provider or worker. Built once per ``Store.open`` (one
+    ``StoreIndex.build`` pass), reused for every revision on that sheet.
+    """
+
+    def __init__(self, store: Store) -> None:
+        self._store = store
+        self._index = StoreIndex.build(store)
+
+    def index(self) -> StoreIndex:
+        return self._index
+
+    def record(self, key: ResourceKey):
+        return self._store.get(key)
+
+    def read_array(self, ref):
+        return self._store.read_array(ref)
+
+
+@contextmanager
+def open_h2_store(state_dir: Path) -> Iterator[Store]:
+    """READ-ONLY: ``Store.open`` directly (module docstring)."""
+    registry = record_registry(page_domain=())
+    with Store.open(state_dir, registry, fsync=False) as store:
+        yield store
+
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# per-sheet geometry helpers (frame/prepared-plane, no raster required)
+# ===========================================================================
+
+
+class SheetPixels:
+    """The capture/region/footing facts + prepared-plane cache one sheet's
+    pass reads pixels through — ``solve.plane_pixels.PlanePixels``'s
+    reuse-only path (module docstring), replicated on bare records
+    because that mixin lives on a full ``SessionPlane`` this script does
+    not build (RULINGS discipline: ``Store.open``, never
+    ``cli.open_receiver``)."""
+
+    def __init__(self, store: Store, row, state_dir: Path) -> None:
+        captures = catalog_captures(store)
+        if len(captures) != 1:
+            raise ValueError(
+                f"{state_dir}: expected exactly one capture, found "
+                f"{len(captures)}")
+        self.cv = capture_view(row, captures[0], captures[0].record.dpi_true)
+        self.region_by_id = {rv.region_id: rv for rv in self.cv.regions}
+        self.footings_by_id = {f.footing_id: f for f in self.cv.footings}
+        self.native_ppc = (self.cv.footings[-1].ppc if self.cv.footings
+                           else None)
+        self.directory = prepared_directory(state_dir)
+        self.config = PlacementConfig()
+        self._prepared: dict = {}
+        self._raw_plans: dict = {}
+
+    def frame(self, footing_id) -> FootingFrame:
+        fs = self.footings_by_id[footing_id]
+        if fs.ppc >= self.native_ppc:
+            return FootingFrame.native(self.cv.record.shape_px)
+        return FootingFrame.of(fs.ppc, self.native_ppc, self.cv.record.shape_px)
+
+    def is_native(self, footing_id) -> bool:
+        return self.footings_by_id[footing_id].ppc >= self.native_ppc
+
+    def prepared(self, region_id, footing_id):
+        key = (region_id, footing_id)
+        cached = self._prepared.get(key)
+        if cached is not None:
+            return cached
+        region = self.region_by_id[region_id]
+        frame = self.frame(footing_id)
+        pitch = frame.pitch_px(float(region.lattice.pitch_px))
+        plane = open_prepared_region(
+            self.cv.record.shape_px, region.candidate.support, 0, pitch,
+            config=self.config, backing=self.cv.record.platen_backing,
+            capture_sha256=region.capture_sha256, directory=self.directory,
+            frame=frame)
+        self._prepared[key] = (plane, frame)
+        return plane, frame
+
+    def sub_native_raster(self, footing_id):
+        """The derived rung raster ALREADY on disk, or ``None`` (native,
+        or the derived file is missing). Never opens the scan file."""
+        if self.is_native(footing_id):
+            return None
+        cached = self._raw_plans.get(footing_id)
+        if cached is not None:
+            return cached
+        frame = self.frame(footing_id)
+        plan = footing_plan(self.cv.record.source_sha256, frame.transform,
+                            self.cv.record.shape_px, self.cv.record.dtype,
+                            directory=self.directory)
+        raster = open_footing_raster(plan, self.footings_by_id[footing_id].ppc)
+        self._raw_plans[footing_id] = raster
+        return raster
+
+
+def sample_v1_style(raster, frame: FootingFrame, plane,
+                    native_affine: tuple, cells: np.ndarray
+                    ) -> tuple[float, float] | None:
+    """Arm B (row 12): v1's OWN photometry — no support fill, ``cval`` =
+    the crop's own median (``certified_refine.prepare_region_image`` +
+    ``_sample``) — against arm A (``plane.filtered``, holo2's
+    support-filled prepared plane), on the SAME sample points. Returns
+    (mean |Δ|, max |Δ|), or ``None`` if the raster has no pixels here.
+
+    Cell -> native pixel is ``page_affine_terms``'s own convention
+    (module: "cell (cy,cx) names the corner... every sampler adds the
+    sub-cell offset itself") — ``(cell + 0.5) @ M.T + O`` — the same
+    expression ``v1audit/c1p8_photometry.py`` uses for the SAME reason.
+    """
+    a = np.asarray(native_affine, np.float64).reshape(2, 3)
+    pts_native = (cells.astype(np.float64) + 0.5) @ a[:, :2].T + a[:, 2]
+    pts = frame.transform.source_to_view_points(pts_native)
+    local_a = pts - np.asarray((plane.y0, plane.x0), np.float64)
+    means_a = ndimage.map_coordinates(plane.filtered, local_a.T, order=1,
+                                      cval=plane.backing)
+
+    halo = int(np.ceil(APERTURE_CELLS * plane.pitch_prior)) + 2
+    y0 = max(0, int(np.floor(pts[:, 0].min())) - halo)
+    x0 = max(0, int(np.floor(pts[:, 1].min())) - halo)
+    y1 = min(raster.shape[0], int(np.ceil(pts[:, 0].max())) + halo)
+    x1 = min(raster.shape[1], int(np.ceil(pts[:, 1].max())) + halo)
+    if y1 <= y0 or x1 <= x0:
+        return None
+    raw = np.asarray(raster.crop_luma(y0, y1, x0, x1), np.float32)
+    aperture_px = int(plane.aperture_px)
+    filt_raw = ndimage.uniform_filter(raw, size=aperture_px, mode="nearest")
+    loc = pts - np.asarray((y0, x0), np.float64)
+    means_b = ndimage.map_coordinates(filt_raw, loc.T, order=1,
+                                      cval=float(np.median(raw)))
+    delta = np.abs(means_b - means_a)
+    return float(delta.mean()), float(delta.max())
+
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# the report shapes
+# ===========================================================================
+
+
+@dataclass
+class GateFlipRow:
+    window_id: str
+    footing_id: str
+    base_pose: str
+    revision_pose: str
+    n_cells: int
+    n_valid: int
+    n_pilots_valid: int
+    base_loss_a: float
+    cand_loss_a: float
+    adopted_a: bool
+    base_loss_b: float
+    cand_loss_b: float
+    adopted_b: bool
+    flip: bool
+    ctx_fit_nonzero: bool      # the pool had an adopted fit (nonzero offsets)
+
+
+@dataclass
+class Row54Sample:
+    window_id: str
+    footing_id: str
+    support_count: int
+    observed_count: int
+    deficit: int
+    deficit_frac: float
+
+
+@dataclass
+class Row12Sample:
+    window_id: str
+    footing_id: str
+    pose: str
+    n_cells: int
+    mean_abs_delta: float
+    max_abs_delta: float
+
+
+@dataclass
+class SheetReport:
+    label: str
+    state_dir: str
+    format_ref: str
+    n_windows_with_2_poses: int
+    n_scored: int
+    n_skipped: int
+    skip_reasons: dict
+    flips: int
+    rows: list        # GateFlipRow
+    quarantine_checked_poses: int
+    quarantine_diff_poses: int
+    quarantine_missing_pieces: int
+    row54_samples: list       # Row54Sample
+    row12_sub_native: list    # Row12Sample
+    row12_native_skipped: int
+
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# the per-sheet pass
+# ===========================================================================
+
+
+def analyze_sheet(state_dir: Path, format_ref: str, *, label: str,
+                  pages: int = 1, row54_sample: int = 200,
+                  seed: int = 20260828) -> SheetReport:
+    row = format_row_for(format_ref, pages)
+    spec = tile_format_for(row)
+    base_field = V1ReferenceField(spec)
+    labels_src = CertifiedLabelSource(base_field)
+
+    with open_h2_store(state_dir) as store:
+        plane = ReadOnlyPlane(store)
+        index = plane.index()
+        pixels = SheetPixels(store, row, state_dir)
+
+        multi = {w: keys for w, keys in index.poses_by_window.items()
+                 if len(keys) >= 2}
+        if any(len(keys) > 2 for keys in multi.values()):
+            raise ValueError(
+                f"{state_dir}: a window carries more than two committed "
+                "poses — this script's base/revision split assumes "
+                "exactly two (RULINGS: 'never a third pose, measured')")
+
+        rows: list[GateFlipRow] = []
+        skip_reasons: dict[str, int] = {}
+        flips = 0
+
+        for window_id, keys in sorted(multi.items()):
+            live = index.live_pose(window_id)
+            base_id = next(k for k in keys if k != live)
+            revision_id = live
+            footing_id, region_id, _extent = parse_window_key(window_id)
+            pose_base = index.poses[base_id]
+            pose_revision = index.poses[revision_id]
+
+            found = refine.reach(plane, base_id)
+            cells, calibration_id = refine.PoseRefineWorker._observed(
+                plane, found.pieces)
+            if not cells.size or calibration_id is None:
+                skip_reasons["no_observed_cells"] = (
+                    skip_reasons.get("no_observed_cells", 0) + 1)
+                continue
+            calibration = refine.replay_calibration(
+                plane, window_id, calibration_id)
+            if calibration is None:
+                skip_reasons["no_calibration"] = (
+                    skip_reasons.get("no_calibration", 0) + 1)
+                continue
+            prepared, frame = pixels.prepared(region_id, footing_id)
+            if prepared is None:
+                skip_reasons["no_prepared_plane"] = (
+                    skip_reasons.get("no_prepared_plane", 0) + 1)
+                continue
+
+            segment, local = refine.local_segment(
+                pose_base.native_affine, frame, cells)
+            means_base = refine.sample_at(
+                prepared.filtered, (prepared.y0, prepared.x0),
+                prepared.backing, segment.pose, local)
+            segment_rev, local_rev = refine.local_segment(
+                pose_revision.native_affine, frame, cells)
+            assert np.array_equal(local, local_rev), (
+                "local_segment's cell correspondence is a pure "
+                "translation (refine_fit module docstring); a mismatch "
+                "here means the base/revision cell sets disagree")
+            means_revision = refine.sample_at(
+                prepared.filtered, (prepared.y0, prepared.x0),
+                prepared.backing, segment_rev.pose, local)
+
+            labels = refine.collect_labels(
+                pose_base.page, cells, base_field, labels_src.field(plane))
+            supported, reason, _counts = refine.support_metrics(labels)
+            if not supported:
+                skip_reasons[reason] = skip_reasons.get(reason, 0) + 1
+                continue
+            valid = refine.select_pose_sites(labels, validation=True)
+            valid_pilots = valid[labels.is_pilot[valid]]
+            if valid_pilots.size < refine.MIN_POSE_PILOTS:
+                skip_reasons["insufficient_pose_pilot_validation"] = (
+                    skip_reasons.get("insufficient_pose_pilot_validation", 0)
+                    + 1)
+                continue
+
+            valid_rows = labels.rows[valid]
+            valid_values = labels.values[valid]
+            valid_weights = labels.weights[valid]
+            pilot_rows = labels.rows[valid_pilots]
+            pilot_values = labels.values[valid_pilots]
+            midpoint = float(np.median(means_base))
+            base_raw_mismatch = float(np.mean(
+                (means_base[pilot_rows] < midpoint) != (pilot_values > 0)))
+            cand_raw_mismatch = float(np.mean(
+                (means_revision[pilot_rows] < midpoint)
+                != (pilot_values > 0)))
+            gi = GateInputs(valid_rows, valid_values, valid_weights,
+                            pilot_rows, pilot_values, base_raw_mismatch,
+                            cand_raw_mismatch)
+
+            def logits_of(means: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+                return np.asarray(
+                    calibration.llr(-np.asarray(means, np.float64)),
+                    np.float64)
+
+            base_logits_a = logits_of(means_base)
+            cand_logits_a = logits_of(means_revision)
+            adopted_a, base_loss_a, cand_loss_a = score_and_gate(
+                base_logits_a, cand_logits_a, gi)
+
+            scope = cal_mod.pose_pool_scope(base_id)
+            pool = cal_mod.ctx_pool_key(*scope) if scope is not None else None
+            fit = (ctx_apply.adopted_context_fit(plane, pool)
+                  if pool is not None else None)
+            offsets = (fit.offsets if fit is not None
+                      else np.zeros(CTX_BINS, np.float64))
+            base_logits_b = ctx_corrected_logits(base_logits_a, cells, offsets)
+            cand_logits_b = ctx_corrected_logits(cand_logits_a, cells, offsets)
+            adopted_b, base_loss_b, cand_loss_b = score_and_gate(
+                base_logits_b, cand_logits_b, gi)
+
+            if not adopted_a:
+                print(f"WARNING {label} {window_id}: as-shipped gate did "
+                     "NOT reproduce adoption on replay (see module "
+                     "docstring point 4)", file=sys.stderr)
+
+            flip = is_flip(adopted_a, adopted_b)
+            flips += int(flip)
+            rows.append(GateFlipRow(
+                window_id=str(window_id), footing_id=str(footing_id),
+                base_pose=str(base_id), revision_pose=str(revision_id),
+                n_cells=int(cells.shape[0]), n_valid=int(valid_rows.size),
+                n_pilots_valid=int(pilot_rows.size),
+                base_loss_a=base_loss_a, cand_loss_a=cand_loss_a,
+                adopted_a=adopted_a, base_loss_b=base_loss_b,
+                cand_loss_b=cand_loss_b, adopted_b=adopted_b, flip=flip,
+                ctx_fit_nonzero=bool(np.any(offsets != 0.0))))
+
+        # ---- row 54: quarantine-blind vs quarantine-filtered, EXHAUSTIVE
+        all_by_pose: dict[ResourceKey, list[ResourceKey]] = {}
+        for key in index.evidence_footings:
+            if key.kind != KIND_EVIDENCE or len(key.parts) != EVIDENCE_KEY_PARTS:
+                continue
+            pose = ResourceKey(
+                KIND_POSE, key.parts[EVIDENCE_KEY_PARTS - POSE_KEY_PARTS:])
+            all_by_pose.setdefault(pose, []).append(key)
+        filtered_map = refine.reaches(plane)     # one pass, all poses
+        q_checked = len(all_by_pose)
+        q_diff_poses = 0
+        q_missing_pieces = 0
+        for pose_id, pieces in all_by_pose.items():
+            filt = filtered_map.get(pose_id)
+            filt_pieces = filt.pieces if filt is not None else ()
+            missing = quarantine_missing(pieces, filt_pieces)
+            if missing:
+                q_diff_poses += 1
+                q_missing_pieces += len(missing)
+
+        # ---- row 54: support-vs-observed cardinality, SAMPLED
+        row54_rows: list[Row54Sample] = []
+        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)
+        all_poses_sorted = sorted(index.poses.keys())
+        n_sample = min(row54_sample, len(all_poses_sorted))
+        for i in rng.choice(len(all_poses_sorted), size=n_sample,
+                            replace=False):
+            pose_id = all_poses_sorted[i]
+            found = filtered_map.get(pose_id)
+            pieces = found.pieces if found is not None else ()
+            cells_i, _cal = refine.PoseRefineWorker._observed(plane, pieces)
+            w_id = ResourceKey(KIND_WINDOW, pose_id.parts[:WINDOW_KEY_PARTS])
+            f_id, r_id, extent = parse_window_key(w_id)
+            region = pixels.region_by_id.get(r_id)
+            if region is None or region.support is None:
+                continue
+            cy0, cx0, cy1, cx1 = extent
+            support_count = int(np.count_nonzero(
+                region.support[cy0:cy1, cx0:cx1]))
+            observed_count = int(cells_i.shape[0])
+            deficit, frac = support_deficit(support_count, observed_count)
+            row54_rows.append(Row54Sample(
+                window_id=str(w_id), footing_id=str(f_id),
+                support_count=support_count, observed_count=observed_count,
+                deficit=deficit, deficit_frac=frac))
+
+        # ---- row 12: arm-A/arm-B on the revised population's own cells,
+        # sub-native footings only (raw pixels already on disk)
+        row12_rows: list[Row12Sample] = []
+        row12_native_skipped = 0
+        for window_id, keys in sorted(multi.items()):
+            footing_id, region_id, _extent = parse_window_key(window_id)
+            if pixels.is_native(footing_id):
+                row12_native_skipped += 1
+                continue
+            live = index.live_pose(window_id)
+            base_id = next(k for k in keys if k != live)
+            pose_base = index.poses[base_id]
+            found = refine.reach(plane, base_id)
+            cells, _cal = refine.PoseRefineWorker._observed(
+                plane, found.pieces)
+            if not cells.size:
+                continue
+            prepared, frame = pixels.prepared(region_id, footing_id)
+            raster = pixels.sub_native_raster(footing_id)
+            if prepared is None or raster is None:
+                continue
+            got = sample_v1_style(raster, frame, prepared,
+                                  pose_base.native_affine, cells)
+            if got is None:
+                continue
+            mean_abs, max_abs = got
+            row12_rows.append(Row12Sample(
+                window_id=str(window_id), footing_id=str(footing_id),
+                pose=str(base_id), n_cells=int(cells.shape[0]),
+                mean_abs_delta=mean_abs, max_abs_delta=max_abs))
+
+    return SheetReport(
+        label=label, state_dir=str(state_dir), format_ref=format_ref,
+        n_windows_with_2_poses=len(multi), n_scored=len(rows),
+        n_skipped=sum(skip_reasons.values()), skip_reasons=skip_reasons,
+        flips=flips, rows=rows,
+        quarantine_checked_poses=q_checked,
+        quarantine_diff_poses=q_diff_poses,
+        quarantine_missing_pieces=q_missing_pieces,
+        row54_samples=row54_rows, row12_sub_native=row12_rows,
+        row12_native_skipped=row12_native_skipped)
+
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# report rendering
+# ===========================================================================
+
+
+def _pct(values, q) -> float:
+    return float(np.percentile(np.asarray(values, np.float64), q)) \
+        if len(values) else float("nan")
+
+
+def render_report(reports: list) -> str:
+    lines: list[str] = ["# RF1 gate flips — row 5 / row 54 / row 12 (M1)", ""]
+    for r in reports:
+        lines.append(f"## {r.label}  (`{r.state_dir}`, `{r.format_ref}`)")
+        lines.append("")
+        lines.append("### Row 5 — the adoption-gate re-score")
+        lines.append(
+            f"- windows with a committed revision (base + live pose): "
+            f"**{r.n_windows_with_2_poses}**")
+        lines.append(
+            f"- scored: {r.n_scored}, skipped: {r.n_skipped} "
+            f"{r.skip_reasons if r.skip_reasons else ''}")
+        lines.append(f"- **FLIPS (a) adopted / (b) refused: {r.flips}**")
+        if r.rows:
+            gain_a = [row.base_loss_a - row.cand_loss_a for row in r.rows]
+            gain_b = [row.base_loss_b - row.cand_loss_b for row in r.rows]
+            n_offset = sum(1 for row in r.rows
+                          if row.ctx_fit_nonzero)
+            lines.append(
+                f"- {n_offset}/{len(r.rows)} revisions' pool had an "
+                "adopted (nonzero) context fit")
+            lines.append(
+                "- held-out gain (base_loss − cand_loss), nats — "
+                f"gate (a) marginal: min {min(gain_a):.4f} / "
+                f"p25 {_pct(gain_a,25):.4f} / median {_pct(gain_a,50):.4f} "
+                f"/ p75 {_pct(gain_a,75):.4f} / max {max(gain_a):.4f}")
+            lines.append(
+                "- held-out gain, gate (b) v1-faithful ctx-corrected: "
+                f"min {min(gain_b):.4f} / p25 {_pct(gain_b,25):.4f} / "
+                f"median {_pct(gain_b,50):.4f} / p75 {_pct(gain_b,75):.4f} "
+                f"/ max {max(gain_b):.4f}")
+            deltas = [b - a for a, b in zip(gain_a, gain_b)]
+            lines.append(
+                "- (b) − (a) shift from context correction: "
+                f"min {min(deltas):.4f} / median {_pct(deltas,50):.4f} / "
+                f"max {max(deltas):.4f}  (MIN_HELDOUT_GAIN = "
+                f"{refine.MIN_HELDOUT_GAIN})")
+        lines.append("")
+        lines.append("### Row 54 — is `_observed` complete?")
+        lines.append(
+            f"- quarantine-blind vs quarantine-filtered, ALL "
+            f"{r.quarantine_checked_poses} evidence-owning poses: "
+            f"**{r.quarantine_diff_poses} poses differ, "
+            f"{r.quarantine_missing_pieces} pieces removed by quarantine**")
+        if r.row54_samples:
+            deficits = [s.deficit_frac for s in r.row54_samples
+                       if np.isfinite(s.deficit_frac)]
+            over = sum(1 for s in r.row54_samples if s.deficit < 0)
+            lines.append(
+                f"- support-vs-observed cardinality, "
+                f"{len(r.row54_samples)}-pose sample: deficit as a "
+                f"fraction of support — min {min(deficits):.4f} / "
+                f"median {_pct(deficits,50):.4f} / max {max(deficits):.4f}; "
+                f"{over} poses observed MORE cells than support "
+                "(frame mismatch, would need investigation)")
+        lines.append("")
+        lines.append("### Row 12 — RF1's photometry input, arm A vs arm B")
+        if r.row12_sub_native:
+            means = [s.mean_abs_delta for s in r.row12_sub_native]
+            maxes = [s.max_abs_delta for s in r.row12_sub_native]
+            lines.append(
+                f"- sub-native-footing revisions compared: "
+                f"{len(r.row12_sub_native)} "
+                f"(native-footing revisions NOT compared, no on-disk raw "
+                f"pixels: {r.row12_native_skipped})")
+            lines.append(
+                f"- mean |Δ| per window: min {min(means):.6g} / "
+                f"median {_pct(means,50):.6g} / max {max(means):.6g}")
+            lines.append(
+                f"- max |Δ| per window: min {min(maxes):.6g} / "
+                f"median {_pct(maxes,50):.6g} / max {max(maxes):.6g}")
+        else:
+            lines.append("- no sub-native-footing revisions in this sheet")
+        lines.append("")
+    return "\n".join(lines)
+
+
+# ===========================================================================
+# CLI
+# ===========================================================================
+
+
+def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
+        description=__doc__.splitlines()[0],
+        formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
+    parser.add_argument("--sheet", choices=(*SHEETS, "all"), default="all")
+    parser.add_argument("--state", type=Path, default=None,
+                        help="override the archived state dir (single "
+                             "--sheet only)")
+    parser.add_argument("--format", default=None,
+                        help="override the format ref (single --sheet "
+                             "only, default matches SHEETS)")
+    parser.add_argument("--row54-sample", type=int, default=200)
+    parser.add_argument("--out", type=Path, default=None,
+                        help="write the markdown report here (also "
+                             "printed to stdout); a sibling .json carries "
+                             "every per-window row")
+    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
+
+    names = list(SHEETS) if args.sheet == "all" else [args.sheet]
+    if args.state is not None and len(names) != 1:
+        parser.error("--state requires a single --sheet")
+
+    reports = []
+    for name in names:
+        cfg = SHEETS[name]
+        state_dir = args.state or Path(cfg["state"])
+        format_ref = args.format or cfg["fmt"]
+        print(f"# {name}: {state_dir}", file=sys.stderr)
+        reports.append(analyze_sheet(
+            state_dir, format_ref, label=name,
+            row54_sample=args.row54_sample))
+
+    text = render_report(reports)
+    print(text)
+    if args.out is not None:
+        args.out.write_text(text, encoding="utf-8")
+        json_path = args.out.with_suffix(".json")
+        json_path.write_text(
+            json.dumps([asdict(r) for r in reports], indent=1, default=str),
+            encoding="utf-8")
+        print(f"\nwrote {args.out}\nwrote {json_path}", file=sys.stderr)
+    return 0
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    raise SystemExit(main())
